WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.941 --> 00:00:14.403
is the greatest love story ever told, or at least the most famous.

2
00:00:15.063 --> 00:00:20.286
As you would expect with such a great romance, it has young lovers, secret meetings, aching hearts, and

3
00:00:20.346 --> 00:00:21.587
flowery words of passion.

4
00:00:22.247 --> 00:00:27.070
Sadly, this story is also a tragedy, and our two young heroes must also learn the cruel fate

5
00:00:27.290 --> 00:00:30.532
that awaits tragic lovers but that's getting ahead of the story.

6
00:00:30.964 --> 00:00:33.726
Let's start at the beginning of the Tragedy of Romeo and Juliet.

7
00:00:34.287 --> 00:00:39.071
Our story is set in Verona, where the city's two chief families, the Capulets and the Montagues, were

8
00:00:39.131 --> 00:00:44.996
enemies. There had been an old quarrel between these families, which grew so great that it extended even

9
00:00:45.036 --> 00:00:46.237
to the most distant cousin.

10
00:00:46.817 --> 00:00:50.921
In fact, not even a servant of the house of Montague could meet a servant of the house

11
00:00:50.961 --> 00:00:53.923
of Capulet without fierce words and sometimes bloodshed.

12
00:00:55.705 --> 00:01:00.948
One morning the son of Lord Montague, Romeo, met his friend Benvolio, who had just witnessed one of

13
00:01:00.988 --> 00:01:05.209
the frequent brawls between the Capulets and Montagues that too often disturbed the city.

14
00:01:05.870 --> 00:01:10.111
And because Benvolio was a Montague as well, he had almost been caught up in the fight.

15
00:01:10.131 --> 00:01:12.551
"Good morning, cousin," he greeted Romeo.

16
00:01:12.571 --> 00:01:13.752
"Is it still morning?

17
00:01:14.172 --> 00:01:15.472
How can the day be so young?"

18
00:01:16.032 --> 00:01:19.313
Romeo wondered, too preoccupied to notice his friend's excitement.

19
00:01:19.333 --> 00:01:21.874
"Why, it's only nine o'clock," Benvolio answered.

20
00:01:22.554 --> 00:01:26.195
Almost to himself, Romeo sighed, "Sad hours seem long."

21
00:01:26.215 --> 00:01:29.276
"Romeo, what sadness so lengthens your hours?"

22
00:01:30.088 --> 00:01:30.649
"I'm in love.

23
00:01:30.869 --> 00:01:33.171
But alas, I'm out of favor with the woman I love.

24
00:01:33.571 --> 00:01:34.692
Rosaline doesn't love me."

25
00:01:35.353 --> 00:01:36.794
Benvolio suspected as much.

26
00:01:37.375 --> 00:01:42.620
Romeo had a passionate heart, and Benvolio had often seen him walking alone under the city's sycamore trees

27
00:01:42.680 --> 00:01:49.346
sighing. He was trying to cheer up Romeo when they were interrupted by a messenger carrying an invitation

28
00:01:49.386 --> 00:01:50.447
to a costumed dance.

29
00:01:51.187 --> 00:01:55.191
The servant asked them if they knew where to find the gentlemen and ladies whose names were written

30
00:01:55.231 --> 00:01:56.052
on the sheet of paper.

31
00:01:56.768 --> 00:02:00.589
Looking at the invitation, Romeo noticed the name of the hard-hearted Rosaline.

32
00:02:00.609 --> 00:02:03.330
"Here is your cure," suggested Benvolio.

33
00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:05.090
"We shall go to the dance.

34
00:02:05.571 --> 00:02:09.232
You'll conclude that your swan is no better than a crow when you see her among all the

35
00:02:09.292 --> 00:02:11.192
other beauties of Verona."

36
00:02:11.212 --> 00:02:15.353
Romeo had little faith in Benvolio's words, but he was happy to go just for the chance to

37
00:02:15.433 --> 00:02:16.254
see his "swan."

38
00:02:16.274 --> 00:02:18.974
"You two are most welcome," said the messenger.

39
00:02:18.994 --> 00:02:23.856
"My master is the rich Lord Capulet, and any who are not of the house of Montague may

40
00:02:23.916 --> 00:02:27.453
attend." "How can we go to a dance at Lord Capulet's?"

41
00:02:28.053 --> 00:02:30.455
said Romeo after they had sent the messenger on his way.

42
00:02:30.475 --> 00:02:35.157
"The prince of the city has ordered that our quarrelsome families should not disturb the peace again.

43
00:02:35.698 --> 00:02:38.019
If a brawl breaks out, our lives will be forfeit!"

44
00:02:38.039 --> 00:02:41.521
"It is a costumed dance," pointed out Benvolio.

45
00:02:41.541 --> 00:02:44.502
"We can wear masks, and they will gain us entrance."

46
00:02:45.143 --> 00:02:50.265
So that evening, young Romeo and Benvolio, along with their friend Mercutio, went to the dance dressed in

47
00:02:50.325 --> 00:02:51.366
costumes and masks.

48
00:02:52.426 --> 00:02:57.678
At Lord Capulet's house, as the guests were arriving, Lady Capulet called for her daughter, Juliet.

49
00:02:57.698 --> 00:03:00.841
"I am here, Mother," said Juliet, arriving with her nurse.

50
00:03:00.861 --> 00:03:01.841
"What is your will?"

51
00:03:02.902 --> 00:03:04.083
Lady Capulet paused.

52
00:03:04.403 --> 00:03:05.685
She wasn't sure how to begin.

53
00:03:05.705 --> 00:03:08.887
"Nurse, you've known Juliet since she was just a baby.

54
00:03:09.147 --> 00:03:09.848
How old is she?"

55
00:03:09.868 --> 00:03:16.714
"Well, the summer festival is in two weeks," began the nurse, "so it's almost her fourteenth birthday.

56
00:03:17.274 --> 00:03:20.937
She was the sweetest little baby, born the night before the festival, as you know.

57
00:03:21.618 --> 00:03:27.097
It was the year after the earthquake, so I remember it well "Stop chattering," interrupted Lady Capulet.

58
00:03:27.117 --> 00:03:28.878
"You can never give a simple answer."

59
00:03:29.218 --> 00:03:29.959
She paused again.

60
00:03:29.979 --> 00:03:32.640
"Tell me, Juliet, how do you feel about marriage?"

61
00:03:33.301 --> 00:03:34.121
Juliet blushed.

62
00:03:34.141 --> 00:03:37.483
"Oh, Mother, it is an honor I haven't even dreamt of."

63
00:03:37.503 --> 00:03:39.764
"Well, you must think of marriage.

64
00:03:40.185 --> 00:03:44.967
Many women younger than you are married ladies now, and the young Count Paris has asked for your

65
00:03:45.007 --> 00:03:47.209
hand. He's coming to the dance tonight."

66
00:03:47.909 --> 00:03:52.732
Juliet politely made no promise but agreed to decide after she saw Count Paris for herself.

67
00:03:53.536 --> 00:03:57.319
"Count Paris is such a gentleman," said the nurse as they walked toward the dance hall.

68
00:03:58.740 --> 00:04:03.664
Romeo and his friends entered just as Lord Capulet called out, "Come, musicians, play!"

69
00:04:04.064 --> 00:04:05.385
and the lively music started.

70
00:04:05.925 --> 00:04:10.309
Romeo's friends rushed toward the dance floor, but he wanted to stay by the door to watch.

71
00:04:10.929 --> 00:04:13.151
"You two go ahead," Romeo encouraged them.

72
00:04:13.171 --> 00:04:15.352
"Tickle the dance floor with your toes."

73
00:04:16.093 --> 00:04:20.016
Then he leaned against a column and watched the dancers step and sway and twirl.

74
00:04:20.948 --> 00:04:24.811
Juliet had left her nurse and was one of the first onto the floor as well.

75
00:04:25.412 --> 00:04:28.715
Gradually the patterns of the dance brought her in front of Romeo's eyes.

76
00:04:29.235 --> 00:04:31.878
When he saw her, he felt as though his heart had stopped.

77
00:04:31.898 --> 00:04:33.659
"What lady is that?"

78
00:04:34.019 --> 00:04:36.081
Romeo quickly asked a passing serving man.

79
00:04:36.101 --> 00:04:40.525
"She's so glorious she even teaches the torches how to burn bright."

80
00:04:41.466 --> 00:04:43.628
But he didn't bother to listen to the servant's answer.

81
00:04:44.108 --> 00:04:45.369
His heart was already caught.

82
00:04:45.389 --> 00:04:47.291
"Did my heart love before?"

83
00:04:47.711 --> 00:04:48.432
he said out loud.

84
00:04:50.164 --> 00:04:53.766
"If it did, I deny it, for I never saw true beauty until this night."

85
00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:58.089
When the song ended, he stepped out into the crowd to find the beautiful girl.

86
00:04:58.969 --> 00:05:05.133
At just that moment, Tybalt, a hot-headed nephew of Lady Capulet, had been standing behind Romeo and recognized

87
00:05:05.193 --> 00:05:05.653
his voice.

88
00:05:05.673 --> 00:05:10.176
"How dare Romeo, that sneaking Montague, come into this house!"

89
00:05:10.596 --> 00:05:12.617
he snarled and pulled out his sword.

90
00:05:14.158 --> 00:05:16.719
But his uncle saw him and warned him to put his weapon away.

91
00:05:17.804 --> 00:05:20.406
"Tybalt, I won't let you cause an uproar among my guests!"

92
00:05:20.786 --> 00:05:21.367
he scolded.

93
00:05:22.287 --> 00:05:26.891
Furious, Tybalt was forced to be patient, but he swore revenge quietly to himself.

94
00:05:27.731 --> 00:05:29.633
Across the room, Romeo found Juliet.

95
00:05:30.553 --> 00:05:35.477
Knowing that because he wore a mask he could dare to be more forward, he approached and gently

96
00:05:35.537 --> 00:05:36.258
took her hand.

97
00:05:38.479 --> 00:05:40.761
With playful charm, he called her hand a shrine.

98
00:05:40.781 --> 00:05:44.784
"I am a poor pilgrim," he said, "who must kiss this holy shrine."

99
00:05:45.484 --> 00:05:50.468
"Good pilgrim," Juliet replied with a clever smile, "pilgrims should use their lips for prayer."

100
00:05:51.188 --> 00:05:53.790
Romeo removed his mask and looked into her eyes.

101
00:05:53.810 --> 00:05:57.232
"Yes, sweet saint, but lips can pray the way hands do.

102
00:05:57.553 --> 00:06:03.277
Palm to palm, they gently touch," he said and, leaning forward, he gently touched his lips to hers.

103
00:06:03.297 --> 00:06:08.040
"Oh pilgrim, you have sinned," Juliet said, but she was smiling warmly.

104
00:06:08.861 --> 00:06:13.104
Romeo was about to answer with another witty reply when Juliet's nurse interrupted them.

105
00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:19.023
She looked at Romeo's face with surprise and then said, "Juliet, your mother wants a word with you."

106
00:06:20.504 --> 00:06:21.204
"Who is her mother?"

107
00:06:21.484 --> 00:06:23.706
Romeo quickly asked the nurse as they turned to go.

108
00:06:24.426 --> 00:06:28.308
She replied that Juliet's mother was the lady of the house and hurried to catch up.

109
00:06:29.008 --> 00:06:31.470
Romeo's heart stopped for the second time that night.

110
00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.251
"She is a Capulet then!"

111
00:06:33.611 --> 00:06:34.211
he gasped.

112
00:06:34.892 --> 00:06:38.053
Quickly he put his mask over his face again and turned to find the door.

113
00:06:38.894 --> 00:06:42.536
For her part, Juliet was waiting impatiently to ask her nurse the same question.

114
00:06:43.232 --> 00:06:45.994
"That handsome gentleman just leaving now, do you know his name?"

115
00:06:46.655 --> 00:06:48.616
"The young man you were talking with so closely?"

116
00:06:49.136 --> 00:06:49.677
said the nurse.

117
00:06:49.697 --> 00:06:52.659
"Oh Juliet, do not ask after him.

118
00:06:53.139 --> 00:06:55.001
His name is Romeo, and he is a Montague.

119
00:06:55.741 --> 00:06:57.983
He is the only son of your father's great enemy."

120
00:06:58.744 --> 00:06:59.724
Her nurse stared at her.

121
00:06:59.985 --> 00:07:01.366
Juliet's face had turned pale.

122
00:07:01.386 --> 00:07:03.067
"Must I love my enemy?"

123
00:07:03.567 --> 00:07:03.987
she said.
